Deep discharge shortens the lifespan of EV batteries. If the remaining SOC is less than or equal to 0.2 when the EV arrives, it will charge until it reaches 1. If the SOC is above 0.2 when the owner gets home, he should focus on discharging schedules until it drops to 0.2. After that, it goes to charge scheduling until the SOC hits 1. Thus, the most important part of optimization is the timing of the charging and discharging. Accordingly, there are two situations:
