                                                  \begin{document}$$\mathrm{i}\mathrm{r}$$\end{document}) are assumed to be 20 years and 10%, respectively. Accordingly, the capital recovery factor (CRF) is calculated as given in Eq. (37)22. The components of battery, FC, and EL have RC, since their lifespans are shorter than the project lifetime. The RC of each component equals the initial CI. To convert the RC to its present value, the discount factor σ (u) is applied, where u denotes the replacement year, as expressed in Eq. (38)22.37\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
